WEBVTT

00:02.045 --> 00:04.005
[Narrator] Previously on lost:

00:04.088 --> 00:05.215
[Wet thud]

00:07.050 --> 00:09.761
[George] Hang on, Naomi,
we'll get you back here asap.

00:09.844 --> 00:11.054
I'm sorry, George.

00:11.137 --> 00:13.723
Just tell my sister that I love her.

00:15.475 --> 00:19.062
You killed Naomi!
— she wants her people to come here.

00:19.145 --> 00:22.023
And trust me, when they do,
we had better be far away from here.

00:22.106 --> 00:24.901
If you want to live,
you need to come with me.

00:24.984 --> 00:27.362
No one's going anwvhere
with you, John.

00:34.494 --> 00:37.247
What are you doing?
— same thing I've always done, Kate.

00:37.330 --> 00:39.165
Surviving.

00:43.086 --> 00:44.754
Thunder's getting louder.

00:46.005 --> 00:48.049
[Helicopter]

00:53.304 --> 00:55.640
[Static]

00:55.723 --> 00:57.725
[Pinging]

01:01.688 --> 01:04.107
[Man #1 on radio] Sorry, Ron.

01:04.190 --> 01:08.528
Drone's got nothing but seafood
at 5,000 meters below.

01:10.029 --> 01:12.323
You pickin' anything up with yours?

01:13.533 --> 01:14.701
[Ron] Zip.

01:14.784 --> 01:17.912
I'm trying to get her a peek
over this Ridge as soon as I can.

01:17.996 --> 01:20.331
Sonar's pinging up something now.

01:21.332 --> 01:24.127
You want to switch feeds?
— [man #1] Roger that.

01:26.546 --> 01:30.383
I'm headed on a bearing
of about 137

01:30.466 --> 01:33.261
from the coordinates
we pulled off our guy's map,

01:33.344 --> 01:35.346
but don't hold your breath.

01:38.224 --> 01:42.020
Magnetometer's picking up a hell
of a lot of anomalies down here.

01:42.687 --> 01:46.149
[Ron] A chest full of doubloons?
— [man #1] Keep dreaming, Ron.

01:46.232 --> 01:49.235
Let's swing around on the next grid
and recalibrate.

01:51.404 --> 01:53.323
[Ron] Are you getting this?

01:53.406 --> 01:55.700
[Man #1] What? What's up?

01:57.952 --> 02:00.913
[Ron] It's... it's an airplane.

02:06.627 --> 02:08.338
Oh, my god.

02:08.421 --> 02:11.758
It's oceanic 815.

02:17.764 --> 02:21.059
[Woman on TV] This haunting footage
comes to us from the Christiane I,

02:21.142 --> 02:23.102
a salvage vehicle in the Indian ocean.

02:23.186 --> 02:25.772
For more than two months
it's been scouring the depths

02:25.855 --> 02:28.691
of the sunda trench off Bali
in search of the remains

02:28.775 --> 02:30.318
of sunken trading ships.

02:30.401 --> 02:35.823
Late last night the Christiane deployed
two remotely operated vehicles, ro vs,

02:35.907 --> 02:40.703
that verified what the national
transportation safety board long feared,

02:40.787 --> 02:42.747
[woman] How do you want
your eggs, Dan?

02:42.830 --> 02:44.874
- — [Sobs]
- [Woman on TV continues]

02:44.957 --> 02:49.212
So, what happened?
They found that missing plane?

02:49.295 --> 02:52.882
- — Dan?
- Oceanic 815 did crash at sea.

02:52.965 --> 02:56.052
Dan?
— even with this tragic discovery...

02:56.135 --> 02:59.013
Dan, why are you so upset?

03:00.890 --> 03:02.558
I don't know.

03:05.269 --> 03:06.729
[Thunder] — [crackling]

03:08.564 --> 03:10.983
I can't find my vest!
— check under your seat!

03:11.067 --> 03:13.069
[Woman] I already did!
— get ready!

03:13.152 --> 03:16.364
Here, just take mine.
— all right!

03:16.447 --> 03:18.324
Everybody out, now!

03:18.783 --> 03:21.327
Hey, genius! Go! — no! No!

03:22.328 --> 03:25.289
Go! — [Dan shouting]

03:29.919 --> 03:32.672
[Panting]

03:34.173 --> 03:35.967
[Grunting]

03:37.135 --> 03:38.386
[Groans]

03:39.762 --> 03:42.181
- — [Branch snaps]
- [Gaspsi

03:51.107 --> 03:53.192
[Many branches snapping]

03:54.360 --> 03:56.612
[Panting]

04:10.960 --> 04:14.046
Hey, there. Are you Jack?

04:18.176 --> 04:19.844
Yeah. I'm Jack.

04:21.304 --> 04:22.847
Who are you?

04:26.559 --> 04:28.394
I'm Daniel Faraday.

04:32.106 --> 04:33.774
I'm here to rescue you.

05:06.432 --> 05:10.019
Hey, Dan. The chopper,
how many of you were on it?

05:10.102 --> 05:11.854
Uh, four, including me.

05:11.938 --> 05:14.941
So, what happened to the rest of them?

05:15.024 --> 05:17.485
Yeah, yeah. I, uh,
I have no idea.

05:17.568 --> 05:20.530
I don't know how many of them
were able to get out before it...

05:20.613 --> 05:23.491
Went down. I just,
ijumped, and I lost my, uh...

05:23.574 --> 05:26.202
What do you call it? My, my pack.
My phone was in my bag.

05:26.285 --> 05:29.288
If I had my phone, I would just, uh...
— we have a phone.

05:30.831 --> 05:33.125
[Dan] You, you have a phone. Uh...

05:33.751 --> 05:35.836
[Kate chuckles] — thank you.

05:35.920 --> 05:37.922
[Phone beeps]

05:38.881 --> 05:41.384
[George] Minkowski.
— hey, George, it's Daniel.

05:41.467 --> 05:43.511
Dan? The chopper comm went dead.

05:43.594 --> 05:45.763
What happened up there?
— yeah, I don't know.

05:45.846 --> 05:48.891
[Stammers] There was an electrical
storm. All the instruments,

05:48.975 --> 05:52.770
I think they went down. But, listen, I
made contact with some of the survivors,

05:52.853 --> 05:55.815
and, uh, we were just, uh...
— Dan, am I on speaker?

05:59.944 --> 06:03.197
Would you give me just,
just one second? [Scoffs]

06:05.908 --> 06:07.034
[Quietly] Hey...

06:07.118 --> 06:10.329
[Unintelligible]
— don't worry. Naomi covered for us.

06:11.539 --> 06:14.917
They don't know what Locke did to her.
— you sure about that?

06:21.757 --> 06:25.177
Ok, ok, so the boat hasn't heard
from anybody else yet,

06:25.261 --> 06:29.724
but, uh, there are GPS transponders,
my team and I are all wearing these.

06:29.807 --> 06:33.227
The transponders will send
the locations back to the ship,

06:33.311 --> 06:37.773
and the ship will send all locations
back in to the phones.

06:37.857 --> 06:40.318
[Phone beeps]
— uh, that's my signal, right there,

06:40.401 --> 06:43.863
and we'll hopefully get the signals
from the rest of the team soon.

06:43.946 --> 06:47.283
Will you help me find them?
— absolutely.

06:47.366 --> 06:48.451
[Dan] Ok. Thank you.

06:51.704 --> 06:54.582
Hey, where are the rest of your people?

06:54.665 --> 06:58.169
Most of them are back at the beach.
— most of them?

07:13.434 --> 07:17.396
Dude, what's wrong with you?
You're gonna get struck by lightning.

07:21.233 --> 07:22.985
The storm is about to pass, Hugo.

07:23.069 --> 07:25.237
It's a freakin' monsoon. We gotta...

07:32.036 --> 07:33.412
Let's go.

07:44.090 --> 07:45.549
Why are you going east?

07:45.633 --> 07:48.302
I thought you said the barracks
were due south.

07:48.386 --> 07:50.888
Because, James, we have to make
a little detour first.

07:50.971 --> 07:54.850
Detour to what?
— there's a cabin I have to go to.

07:54.934 --> 07:57.311
I thought the cabin was back that way.

07:58.270 --> 07:59.730
What did you say, Hugo?

08:03.609 --> 08:06.987
I, uh, thought you were talking
about the airplane cabin.

08:09.615 --> 08:12.326
Why are we wasting our time
going to some shack, anwvay?

08:12.410 --> 08:14.453
Because we're supposed to.
— right.

08:14.537 --> 08:18.124
Like you were supposed to throw
a knife into that Naomi chick's back?

08:23.212 --> 08:26.465
You mind us who you're getting
your orders from, colonel Kurtz?

08:27.842 --> 08:29.468
I got 'em from Walt.

08:43.733 --> 08:45.651
Jack still isn't back.

08:48.320 --> 08:49.947
Anything?

08:50.448 --> 08:53.075
No. But it's a big island.

08:53.159 --> 08:55.995
The freighter could be approaching
from the other side.

08:56.078 --> 08:58.080
That's the spirit.

09:01.000 --> 09:03.419
Juliet, you lived amongst the others.

09:03.502 --> 09:07.173
Why would Ben say the people
coming here intend to do us harm?

09:07.256 --> 09:08.758
Because he's a liar,

09:08.841 --> 09:11.677
and he's trying to scare us.
That's what Ben does.

09:13.971 --> 09:17.641
Or because the people coming here
intend to do us harm.

09:20.895 --> 09:23.022
How many guns do you have left?

09:26.442 --> 09:28.319
[Beeps]

09:36.452 --> 09:39.246
Hey. Is that from your chopper?

09:42.541 --> 09:43.959
Yeah, yeah, that, uh... yeah.

09:44.043 --> 09:47.296
They reduced the weight load
when they started going down.

09:47.379 --> 09:50.591
[Laughs nervously]
Guess that's why they pushed me out.

09:58.933 --> 10:03.312
I'm not in charge of,
uh, packing, so, um...

10:03.395 --> 10:05.981
You're not, huh?
— we should, uh...

10:06.065 --> 10:09.109
Hey, Daniel, why'd you bring the gun?

10:10.903 --> 10:12.154
[Dan] Uh...

10:15.032 --> 10:16.784
Uh, as a precaution.

10:16.867 --> 10:19.411
Precaution against what?

10:24.083 --> 10:26.043
Uh, ok, see, um...

10:27.962 --> 10:30.714
Rescuing you and your people...

10:32.049 --> 10:35.636
I can't really say
it's our primary objective.

10:43.519 --> 10:45.521
[Phone beeps]

10:47.314 --> 10:49.149
[Dan] It's miles.

10:49.233 --> 10:51.944
It's miles. Come on.

10:52.027 --> 10:55.573
What the hell you mean
you saw Walt? In a dream?

10:55.656 --> 10:57.700
No dream. It was Walt.

10:57.783 --> 11:00.661
Only... taller.

11:00.744 --> 11:02.955
Taller? What, like a giant?

11:06.333 --> 11:10.129
Ok, what exactly did Walt tell you?
— he said I had work to do,

11:10.212 --> 11:14.216
that I had to stop this woman Naomi from
bringing the rest of her people here.

11:14.300 --> 11:16.385
You didn't ask him follow—up questions?

11:16.468 --> 11:19.221
Ben had shot me and left me for dead.
Walt saved my life,

11:19.305 --> 11:21.599
so I pretty much took him at his word.

11:22.349 --> 11:23.684
He shot you,

11:23.767 --> 11:27.354
yet here you are, fit as a fiddle,
tromping through the jungle.

11:30.232 --> 11:31.817
The bullet went in one side,

11:31.901 --> 11:33.694
came out the other.

11:41.368 --> 11:44.246
I'd probably be dead
if I still had a kidney there.

11:45.456 --> 11:46.999
Anything else?

12:15.027 --> 12:16.362
He's down there.

12:18.364 --> 12:19.698
Hey, miles!

12:40.469 --> 12:42.054
Back up, handsome.

12:43.138 --> 12:46.809
Wait, whoa, whoa!
Miles, take it easy, it's ok.

12:46.892 --> 12:48.769
They're here to help us.
It's ok, miles.

12:48.852 --> 12:51.981
They're just trying to help.
— hey! Back away from him!

12:52.064 --> 12:54.650
Hands where I can see 'em!
— Kate, it's all right.

12:54.733 --> 12:55.985
It's ok.

12:57.403 --> 12:58.529
You're Kate?

13:00.823 --> 13:02.533
You want to tell me where Naomi is?

13:04.785 --> 13:07.287
What?
— Naomi, the woman you killed.

13:09.540 --> 13:10.582
Where is she?

13:20.342 --> 13:23.804
[Man on TV] For the friends and families
of the passengers of oceanic 815,

13:23.887 --> 13:26.682
this can only be described
as the worst—case scenario.

13:26.765 --> 13:29.685
With the plane accounted for
and a salvage mission unlikely,

13:29.768 --> 13:33.981
authorities are confirming
all 324 passengers dead.

13:48.203 --> 13:50.706
Ms. Gardner, I'm miles Straume.

13:50.789 --> 13:54.334
We spoke on the phone earlier.
— oh, oh, please come in.

14:06.805 --> 14:10.350
Which room is it?
— It's upstairs at the end of the hall.

14:10.976 --> 14:14.563
I get paid in advance.
Two hundred, cash only.

14:14.646 --> 14:15.898
You told me a hundred...

14:15.981 --> 14:19.985
That was before my buddy at the police
told me your grandson was murdered.

14:21.320 --> 14:23.322
It's gonna be two hundred.

14:24.073 --> 14:25.365
Fine.

14:49.098 --> 14:51.850
No matter what you hear,
don't come up.

15:33.892 --> 15:37.604
You're not doing your grandmother
any good staying here, man.

15:37.688 --> 15:40.065
You're causing her a lot of pain.

15:44.736 --> 15:48.073
I... I want to go downstairs
and tell her you've gone,

15:48.157 --> 15:51.535
but the only way
I'm gonna be able to do that

15:51.618 --> 15:54.163
is if you tell me where it is.

15:59.835 --> 16:01.420
So where is it?

16:01.503 --> 16:02.921
[Clattering]

16:38.874 --> 16:40.209
You can go now.

16:47.341 --> 16:48.634
Did it work?

16:53.222 --> 16:55.015
He's at peace now.

17:03.440 --> 17:04.650
Here.

17:06.151 --> 17:07.945
You get a refund. Half off.

17:09.112 --> 17:11.156
Wasn't as tricky as I thought.

17:14.368 --> 17:16.036
Thank you.

17:16.495 --> 17:17.829
Thank you.

17:19.790 --> 17:22.417
Miles. Miles!
Hey, hey, what are you doing?

17:22.501 --> 17:24.586
What are you doing?
These are good people.

17:24.670 --> 17:27.005
Why'd Naomi use the damn code? Yeah.

17:27.089 --> 17:29.883
You remember when she said,
"tell my sister I love her?"

17:29.967 --> 17:32.511
Well, she doesn't have a sister.

17:32.594 --> 17:34.388
That's what we're supposed to say

17:34.471 --> 17:37.099
if we get captured,
have a gun to our heads.

17:37.182 --> 17:41.019
Like right now Jack here would say,
"tell my sister I love her."

17:41.103 --> 17:43.480
You get it?
— we didn't kill your friend.

17:45.107 --> 17:49.069
Then take me to her body.
— miles, what about Charlotte? Frank?

17:49.152 --> 17:52.197
Take me to Naomi.
— Naomi was killed, but not by us.

17:52.281 --> 17:54.950
It was... it was a man
by the name of John Locke.

17:55.033 --> 17:58.078
He's not with us anymore.
— Kate, if I have to ask you again...

17:58.161 --> 18:00.414
Even if I took you to her body
you wouldn't know...

18:00.497 --> 18:01.915
I'll know!

18:03.166 --> 18:05.168
Now take me to her body.

18:24.688 --> 18:26.148
Alex, hey.

18:27.399 --> 18:29.735
What?
— something I need to tell you.

18:29.818 --> 18:31.653
Keep your mouth shut, Mr. Linus.

18:32.738 --> 18:37.367
Karl. Now, if you're gonna sleep with
my daughter I insist you call me Ben.

18:38.368 --> 18:41.538
Easy, kid. Guy'sjust
trying to get in your head.

18:43.665 --> 18:45.250
Go take a walk or something.

18:51.840 --> 18:55.969
Mind if I ask you a question, James?
— yeah, I do.

18:56.678 --> 18:58.180
Why'd you leave Kate behind?

18:58.263 --> 19:01.391
[Scoffs] You're wasting your time, Yoda.

19:02.768 --> 19:05.562
I know it's not pleasant,
but let's face it,

19:05.645 --> 19:08.023
you really don't stand a chance now.

19:09.191 --> 19:10.525
Chance at what?

19:10.609 --> 19:13.862
James, look at yourself.

19:13.945 --> 19:17.366
Yes, on this island,
you're brave, daring, handsome.

19:17.449 --> 19:20.535
You're someone,
but if you left with them...

19:21.536 --> 19:25.123
Back in the real world
a lowlife scam artist like you

19:25.207 --> 19:28.210
could never compete
with a first—class surgeon.

19:29.252 --> 19:33.131
I think Kate was really upset when
you made your choice to come with us.

19:35.467 --> 19:37.886
Thank god she has Jack there
to comfort her...

19:40.931 --> 19:42.140
James!

19:43.308 --> 19:44.893
Don't! — don't what?!

19:45.852 --> 19:48.563
Anyone want to tell me
why we're keeping this guy alive?

19:48.647 --> 19:52.401
We're keeping him alive because
he's been on this island longer than us,

19:52.484 --> 19:54.820
because he has information we need.

19:54.903 --> 19:57.656
Because, apart from his mouth,
he's completely harmless.

19:57.739 --> 19:59.616
His mouth put that hole in your gut?

20:00.909 --> 20:04.955
Ok, James, let's, let's execute him
right here, right now,

20:05.038 --> 20:07.124
in front of his daughter.

20:26.476 --> 20:29.396
It's only a matter of time
before he gets us, Johnny.

20:30.522 --> 20:33.942
And I'll bet he's already figured out
how he's gonna do it.

20:35.861 --> 20:37.863
So you walk him.

21:04.890 --> 21:06.433
What's he doing?

21:08.059 --> 21:09.436
The light...

21:09.519 --> 21:12.105
Is strange out here, isn't it?

21:12.189 --> 21:16.359
It's kind of like it doesn't,
it doesn't scatter

21:16.443 --> 21:17.736
quite right.

21:22.991 --> 21:25.911
Your name is Dan, right? — hmm.

21:26.786 --> 21:31.500
Listen, Dan, I know that you don't
want anybody to get hurt, right?

21:31.583 --> 21:34.628
So why don't you just put that away.

21:36.087 --> 21:40.800
Uh... because, um,
miles would kill me.

21:41.426 --> 21:44.596
We're just trying to help...
— Kate, you're wasting your breath.

21:44.679 --> 21:48.058
Let's just let this play out
and see what happens, ok?

21:53.939 --> 21:56.858
They didn't kill her.
It happened like they said it did.

21:56.942 --> 21:58.276
[Phone beeps] — hey.

21:58.360 --> 22:01.488
[Dan] It's Charlotte. She's only
three kilometers from here.

22:01.571 --> 22:03.448
All right. Let's go get her.

22:05.951 --> 22:08.703
I said let's go.
— you need to put the guns down.

22:08.787 --> 22:11.039
What? — put the guns down.

22:12.624 --> 22:15.794
Now why would I do that?
— our friends are in the jungle now

22:15.877 --> 22:18.547
holding a gun at your head
and his head.

22:19.381 --> 22:22.384
I'll forget about the misunderstanding.
Put the guns down.

22:22.467 --> 22:24.928
Come on, how stupid do you think I am?
— [gunshots]

22:35.480 --> 22:36.982
I don't know, miles.

22:38.441 --> 22:41.027
How stupid are you?

23:00.839 --> 23:03.258
[Chatter]

23:15.520 --> 23:18.231
How many different languages
do you have to read that in

23:18.315 --> 23:20.358
before you believe it's true?

23:20.442 --> 23:22.902
How many different languages are there?

23:24.029 --> 23:27.282
[Man speaks French]

23:27.365 --> 23:29.117
He wants to know if we're lost.

23:29.200 --> 23:32.454
Remind him people in our line
of work are terrible at keeping secrets.

23:32.537 --> 23:35.498
I know about the dig.
— [woman responds in French]

23:38.668 --> 23:42.255
He said the site is closed.
— then tell him to open it.

23:58.271 --> 23:59.606
Dinosaur?

24:01.024 --> 24:02.817
Not by a few million years.

24:02.901 --> 24:04.736
It's an ursus maritimus.

24:04.819 --> 24:07.280
[Woman] Wait, ursus, as in bear?

24:09.491 --> 24:11.242
As in polar bear.

24:13.828 --> 24:17.499
Charlotte, we're in the desert.
This is a hoax, right?

24:21.252 --> 24:23.588
He wants to know what
you're doing with the hammer.

24:23.672 --> 24:24.673
Excavating.

24:24.756 --> 24:28.593
[Man continues in French]

24:31.054 --> 24:32.806
Is that a collar?

24:36.935 --> 24:39.938
[Man continues in French]

24:41.064 --> 24:42.774
[Gasps]

24:59.833 --> 25:01.459
[Groans]

25:31.990 --> 25:33.825
[Gasps]

25:57.015 --> 25:59.017
Hi yourself.

26:06.858 --> 26:08.943
We were worried
when you didn't get back,

26:09.027 --> 26:11.946
so we went out to the cockpit
and tracked you from there.

26:12.030 --> 26:13.990
Thanks for that, for what it's worth.

26:14.073 --> 26:15.074
Don't mention it.

26:15.158 --> 26:18.495
Somebody could've told me
that the cavalry were here.

26:19.287 --> 26:21.790
I gave you that... wink.

26:24.709 --> 26:26.461
What are your names?

26:26.544 --> 26:28.963
Um, I'm Daniel Faraday,
and this is miles...

26:29.047 --> 26:30.548
Don't tell him my last name.

26:31.841 --> 26:33.551
I guess this is just miles.

26:33.635 --> 26:36.638
What do you do for a living, Daniel?
— I'm a physicist.

26:36.721 --> 26:38.556
I guess you can call me a physicist.

26:38.640 --> 26:40.850
I don't really like being pigeonholed...

26:40.934 --> 26:43.812
Dan, you say one more word
and I'll break your fingers.

26:43.895 --> 26:46.564
What do you do, miles?
— I collect soil samples.

26:46.648 --> 26:49.150
Oh, that's nice.
Well, maybe you can help me.

26:49.234 --> 26:51.653
You say you're not here
on a rescue mission,

26:51.736 --> 26:54.364
and the world at large
believes us to be dead.

26:55.365 --> 26:56.991
But here we are, alive and well,

26:57.075 --> 26:59.828
and you don't seem
remotely surprised to see us.

26:59.911 --> 27:04.290
Oh, my god, you guys were on
oceanic flight 815! Wow!

27:04.374 --> 27:05.959
That better?

27:10.213 --> 27:12.215
I can't believe you're alive.

27:14.425 --> 27:16.010
How many of you are there?

27:17.512 --> 27:19.305
Why do you want to know?

27:20.265 --> 27:21.766
Why wouldn't I want to know?

27:25.854 --> 27:27.981
Forty—eight of us survived the crash.

27:28.064 --> 27:30.024
That's not counting the tail section.

27:30.108 --> 27:32.235
They're pretty much dead...
— [Locke] Hugo.

27:33.945 --> 27:36.781
So you've all been living here
this entire time?

27:38.283 --> 27:39.701
Is that your baby?

27:40.952 --> 27:42.620
Yeah. This is Aaron.

27:42.704 --> 27:45.623
Did you have him here on the island?
— mm—hmm.

27:45.707 --> 27:47.292
That's amazing.

27:48.626 --> 27:52.505
Well, I've got about a million
more questions I want to ask you,

27:52.589 --> 27:55.383
but they can wait until
we get you back to the freighter.

27:55.466 --> 27:58.136
We've all got
one of these transponders,

27:58.219 --> 28:00.680
so if we sit tight
they're gonna be here soon, ok?

28:00.763 --> 28:03.641
This team of yours,
how many of you are there?

28:04.642 --> 28:05.894
Four, including me.

28:06.978 --> 28:09.939
What happened to your helicopter?
— I don't know.

28:10.023 --> 28:12.901
The pilot was trying to put it down.
— where?

28:12.984 --> 28:14.986
I don't know.

28:15.069 --> 28:17.530
I had to jump. It was chaos.

28:19.657 --> 28:21.451
I'm lucky to be alive.

28:24.829 --> 28:26.497
Get up. You're coming with us.

28:27.332 --> 28:30.919
What? Why? We need to stay
where we are so that they can find us.

28:31.002 --> 28:32.629
See, there's your problem.

28:32.712 --> 28:34.672
We don't want to be found.

28:38.009 --> 28:39.677
[Phone beeping]

28:39.761 --> 28:42.138
I wouldn't mess around with that
if I were you.

28:42.221 --> 28:44.474
It can't hurt to try and call
someone else.

28:44.557 --> 28:46.267
Oh, it can hurt. — [phone beeps]

28:46.351 --> 28:49.062
What'd you do?
— I didn't do anything.

28:51.272 --> 28:52.857
Your friend Charlotte,

28:52.941 --> 28:55.777
she's moving.
— [beeping accelerates]

28:55.860 --> 28:57.445
And she's moving fast.

29:01.199 --> 29:03.326
She's running from something.

29:30.395 --> 29:32.897
According to this she's right here.

29:33.606 --> 29:35.650
Charlotte? — Charlotte!

29:42.740 --> 29:45.159
[Rustling]

29:45.243 --> 29:46.911
Over there, over there.

29:56.212 --> 29:57.255
Vincent.

30:01.426 --> 30:02.635
Locke's got her.

30:19.277 --> 30:24.032
[Man] We want to caution our viewers
the images are graphic in nature.

30:24.115 --> 30:26.034
Viewer discretion is advised.

30:26.117 --> 30:29.370
Authorities released footage
of the sunken remains

30:29.454 --> 30:32.040
of oceanic flight 815.

30:32.623 --> 30:36.335
The national transportation
safety board has set up a hotline

30:36.419 --> 30:39.672
for family members
of the oceanic victims.

30:39.756 --> 30:43.092
The ntsb has begun
the victim identification process.

30:44.385 --> 30:47.263
We have confirmation
that this is the pilot,

30:47.346 --> 30:50.141
captain Seth Norris.

30:50.224 --> 30:54.145
In a statement,
the ntsb said that,

30:54.228 --> 30:56.773
"due to the sheer depth of the wreck...

30:57.982 --> 31:00.943
Recovery of the bodies
would be next to impossible.

31:01.027 --> 31:04.155
We can only hope that identification
will provide closure

31:04.238 --> 31:06.324
to the families of the victims. ”

31:17.835 --> 31:21.089
[Woman] National transportation safety
board, oceanic hotline.

31:21.172 --> 31:22.840
Let me speak to your supervisor.

31:22.924 --> 31:25.551
Yes, sir. Are you a family member
of the deceased?

31:25.635 --> 31:27.929
No, but I got some information
on the crash.

31:28.012 --> 31:30.598
May I speak to your supervisor?
— sir, if you could...

31:30.681 --> 31:32.725
Look, I'm staring at the television now,

31:32.809 --> 31:36.646
you're broadcasting footage and saying
that's the pilot, Seth Norris.

31:36.729 --> 31:37.730
Yes, sir?

31:37.814 --> 31:39.524
Well, that's not him.

31:41.984 --> 31:43.361
Please hold.

31:44.737 --> 31:46.989
[Man] Who am I speaking with?
— doesn't matter.

31:47.073 --> 31:49.992
You're showing footage of Seth Norris.
That's not him.

31:50.076 --> 31:54.080
He married his high school sweetheart
at 19, he always wore his wedding ring.

31:54.163 --> 31:55.998
There's no ring on that body.

31:56.082 --> 32:00.503
Sir, it's likely the ring fell off...
— I'm telling you that is not him.

32:01.420 --> 32:05.091
And how exactly is it that you know
all about captain Norris?

32:06.717 --> 32:10.555
Because I was supposed to be flying
oceanic 815 on that day.

32:38.416 --> 32:40.501
[Grunts]

32:40.585 --> 32:42.628
[Panting]

32:46.424 --> 32:47.633
[Moos]

33:06.777 --> 33:08.279
[Grunts]

33:19.999 --> 33:22.627
[Panting]

33:33.804 --> 33:34.847
That's them.

33:34.931 --> 33:37.058
That's somebody from my team.

33:42.146 --> 33:45.399
What's wrong with you people?
We're here because of you.

33:45.483 --> 33:47.568
I just almost died jumping out
of a helicopter

33:47.652 --> 33:49.987
because you called us for help.

33:50.154 --> 33:53.241
Maybe we should see
who launched that flare.

33:53.324 --> 33:55.910
They could be hurt, John.
— she's lying.

33:55.993 --> 33:59.538
Whatever they came for, it isn't us.
We keep moving forward as planned.

33:59.622 --> 34:02.750
[Sawyer] Sure. Who are we to argue
with taller ghost Walt?

34:02.833 --> 34:05.544
Do whatever you want.
— I want you to come with us.

34:05.628 --> 34:08.798
I'm not asking for permission.
If you think you're gonna stop me

34:08.881 --> 34:10.758
from getting to my...
— [gunshot]

34:14.679 --> 34:16.138
[Grunts]

34:17.098 --> 34:19.517
[Sawyer] What did you do,
you son of a bitch?

34:24.730 --> 34:26.440
[Gasps]

34:28.734 --> 34:31.112
The vest. — what?

34:48.045 --> 34:50.298
[Dan] Is he alive?
— [Jack] He's got a pulse.

34:52.967 --> 34:54.802
Frank. Hey, hey.

34:54.885 --> 34:56.220
Frank! — [grunts]

34:58.889 --> 35:01.058
Are you ok? What happened?

35:03.561 --> 35:07.148
We got struck by lightning.
— frank, where's Charlotte?

35:07.231 --> 35:10.026
She bailed out just...
Before we went down.

35:10.109 --> 35:13.321
I don't know where she is.
— where's the chopper?

35:13.404 --> 35:14.572
I saw a cow.

35:16.907 --> 35:18.409
Hey! Hey!

35:18.492 --> 35:21.203
Lapidus, where's the chopper?
Where did it crash?

35:21.287 --> 35:24.165
Crash? What the hell kind of pilot
do you think I am?

35:24.248 --> 35:26.709
I put her down safe and sound
right over there.

35:57.114 --> 35:58.783
[Naomi] So this is the team?

35:58.866 --> 36:01.744
[Man] Have you familiarized yourself
with their profiles?

36:01.827 --> 36:03.371
[Naomi] Unfortunately, yes.

36:03.454 --> 36:05.956
These are the wrong people
for a mission like this.

36:06.040 --> 36:09.043
None of them have field experience,
military training.

36:09.126 --> 36:12.421
You can't just drop them in
unprotected. It'll be a disaster.

36:12.505 --> 36:14.840
They are not unprotected.
They have you.

36:14.924 --> 36:17.343
[Scoffs] There's only so much I can do.

36:18.302 --> 36:21.055
Your modesty is positively charming.

36:21.138 --> 36:25.017
This is a high—risk covert op
in unstable territory.

36:25.101 --> 36:28.104
It's dodgy enough without
having to baby—sit a head case,

36:28.187 --> 36:30.314
ghostbuster, anthropologist
and a drunk.

36:30.398 --> 36:32.483
To be fair he is also
a pretty good pilot.

36:32.566 --> 36:33.901
It's madness.

36:33.984 --> 36:36.445
What if we find survivors from 815?

36:36.529 --> 36:38.864
There were no survivors.
— yes, I know.

36:38.948 --> 36:42.410
But what if there are survivors?
— there were no survivors

36:42.493 --> 36:44.161
of oceanic 815.

36:44.245 --> 36:47.248
Don't ask questions.
Just do what you were hired for.

36:47.331 --> 36:50.501
Every member of this team
was selected for a specific purpose.

36:50.584 --> 36:53.712
Everything relies on you
getting them in, getting them out

36:53.796 --> 36:56.340
and preventing anyone
from getting killed.

36:56.424 --> 36:58.259
Think you can do that?

37:01.011 --> 37:02.346
Sure.

37:02.430 --> 37:04.098
Why not?

37:25.870 --> 37:29.582
There's some minor damage, but
the mechanical systems are intact.

37:30.458 --> 37:33.043
So it will fly, then?
— absolutely.

37:34.462 --> 37:36.005
Can I have the phone now?

37:37.047 --> 37:39.592
Tell you what. I'll give you the phone

37:39.675 --> 37:42.303
if you tell me what you people
are doing here.

37:42.386 --> 37:45.598
I'll tell you what we're doing here
if you give me the phone.

37:49.935 --> 37:52.104
Don't say anything about your sister.

37:52.188 --> 37:54.607
[Phone beeps]

37:54.690 --> 37:57.151
[Woman] Hello?
— Regina, it's miles.

37:57.234 --> 37:58.944
I need to talk to minkowski.

37:59.028 --> 38:01.489
Minkowski can't come
to the phone right now.

38:02.364 --> 38:04.283
It's important. Go get him.

38:04.366 --> 38:06.744
Miles, he can't come
to the phone right now.

38:07.828 --> 38:09.997
All right, have him call me
when he can.

38:10.080 --> 38:11.499
I gotta go.

38:14.960 --> 38:17.004
Whoa, whoa! What are you
doing with her?

38:17.087 --> 38:20.424
We're taking her with us.
— what's the point? That's not Naomi.

38:20.508 --> 38:23.093
It's just meat.
— we can't just leave her here.

38:23.177 --> 38:24.595
Miles is right.

38:25.262 --> 38:28.516
We burned up most of the damn fuel
flying around in that storm.

38:28.599 --> 38:31.685
We barely got enough
to get back to the freighter.

38:31.769 --> 38:36.106
We're not gonna carry any unnecessary
weight. I'll take her on the next run.

38:36.190 --> 38:38.108
I promise, Dan.

38:41.278 --> 38:43.697
There's a blanket by my backpack.
Would you get it?

38:45.032 --> 38:47.535
[Lapidus] Look as bad as it feels?

38:47.618 --> 38:49.370
[Juliet] How bad does it feel?

38:49.453 --> 38:51.372
[Chuckles]

38:51.455 --> 38:53.624
What's your name again?
— Juliet.

38:54.667 --> 38:57.419
Juliet. Juliet what?

38:58.462 --> 38:59.880
Juliet Burke.

38:59.964 --> 39:01.840
Juliet Burke.

39:03.467 --> 39:05.427
You weren't on that plane, were you?

39:12.935 --> 39:16.230
This is Juliet,
and she was not on the plane.

39:17.648 --> 39:18.857
What?!

39:20.150 --> 39:21.150
You sure?

39:21.193 --> 39:24.029
You know how many times
I studied that damn manifest?

39:24.113 --> 39:27.116
There's no Juliet Burke on that plane.
She's a native.

39:27.658 --> 39:29.577
Really? Where is he?!

39:29.660 --> 39:31.662
Back off! — where's who?

39:31.745 --> 39:34.498
You want to know why we're here?
I'll tell you why.

39:36.834 --> 39:39.503
We're here for Benjamin Linus.

39:45.509 --> 39:47.469
Now where is he?

39:48.637 --> 39:50.472
James, listen to me, please.

39:50.556 --> 39:53.601
Keep your mouth shut.
— [Locke] Are you ok?

39:53.684 --> 39:56.937
I feel like I've got a cinder block
on my chest, but I'll survive.

39:57.021 --> 40:00.190
I'm sorry you got shot.
I didn't intend for that to happen.

40:00.274 --> 40:03.527
Really? It seemed like you were
about to shoot me yourself.

40:04.486 --> 40:06.280
What good would you be to me dead?

40:06.363 --> 40:09.033
[Sarcastic] I feel much more
comfortable now. Thanks.

40:12.036 --> 40:15.581
I guess this is the part where
I'm supposed to say, "I told you so."

40:16.874 --> 40:18.375
James, I stand corrected.

40:19.126 --> 40:20.628
You want me to do it?

40:21.503 --> 40:24.214
No, it's my mess. I'll clean up.

40:27.801 --> 40:30.638
No! Wait!
— Danielle, escort Alex away from here.

40:30.721 --> 40:32.389
Let's go. Come on. — no! No!

40:32.473 --> 40:33.515
She's right. Let's go.

40:33.599 --> 40:36.143
Anyone who doesn't want to see this
should leave now.

40:36.226 --> 40:37.561
We should talk about this...

40:37.645 --> 40:40.981
Claire, what if one of those bullets
had hit you or the baby?

40:41.065 --> 40:42.691
John, listen.

40:44.151 --> 40:46.362
I have information that you need.

40:47.279 --> 40:48.572
I have answers.

40:51.950 --> 40:53.619
What is the monster?

40:54.745 --> 40:57.414
What?
— the black smoke, the monster.

40:58.082 --> 40:59.416
What is it?

41:00.709 --> 41:02.086
I don't know.

41:03.379 --> 41:06.423
Goodbye, Benjamin.
— her name is Charlotte Lewis!

41:10.761 --> 41:12.846
Charlotte staples Lewis.

41:14.098 --> 41:17.559
Born July 2, 1979,
essex, england.

41:17.643 --> 41:20.854
Parents David and Jeannette.
Eldest of three, all girls.

41:21.689 --> 41:25.025
She was raised in bromsgrove.
Did her undergraduate studies at Kent.

41:25.109 --> 41:28.696
Took her Ph.D.
in cultural anthropology at Oxford.

41:28.779 --> 41:31.532
She's here with two other
team members and a pilot.

41:31.615 --> 41:34.660
Their names: Daniel Faraday,
miles Straume,

41:34.743 --> 41:36.453
frank lapidus.

41:44.420 --> 41:47.214
Your instinct was right, John.

41:47.297 --> 41:49.466
These people are a threat.

41:50.634 --> 41:54.722
If you shoot me, you'll never know
how great a threat they were.

41:54.805 --> 41:57.599
Because I know what they're doing here.

41:57.683 --> 41:59.309
I know what they want.

42:00.310 --> 42:01.812
What do they want?

42:03.897 --> 42:05.983
Me, James. They want me.

42:14.742 --> 42:16.744
How do you know all this?

42:21.123 --> 42:24.001
Because I have a man on their boat.
